GLtron - Installation from source

Requirements:

  - A C99 / C++ compiler (gcc, clang)
  - CMake >= 3.21 and a build tool (Ninja or GNU Make)
  - pkg-config
  - SDL2 (libsdl2-dev / SDL2-devel)
  - SDL2_sound (SDL2_sound-devel)
  - OpenGL (libgl1-mesa-dev or vendor equivalent; the macOS framework is
    used automatically when building on macOS)
  - GLEW (libglew-dev / glew-devel)
  - libpng (libpng-dev / libpng-devel)
  - zlib (zlib1g-dev / zlib-devel)

Optional:

  - SDL2_net (only when building with -DGLTRON_NETWORK=ON)


Building:

  cmake -S . -B build -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release
  cmake --build build -j

Installing (probably as root):

  cmake --install build

Default install prefix is /usr/local. Override with
-DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=/path when configuring.

Data files (art, music, sounds, scripts, levels) are installed under
${prefix}/share/gltron and the binary has that path baked in via
DATA_DIR. The user config file is stored at $HOME/.gltronrc.


CMake options:

  -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Debug|Release|RelWithDebInfo|MinSizeRel
                                       (default: Release)
  -DGLTRON_WARN=ON                     enable -Wall -Werror (default: OFF)
  -DGLTRON_NETWORK=ON                  experimental SDL2_net support
                                       (default: OFF)
  -DGLTRON_SNAPSHOT_DIR=PATH           where screenshots are saved
                                       (default: ~)
  -DGLTRON_PREFERENCES_DIR=PATH        where the prefs file lives
                                       (default: ~)


Container build:

A Fedora-based podman dev container is available via Makefile.docker:

  make -f Makefile.docker image    # build the image (also builds gltron)
  make -f Makefile.docker shell    # drop into a shell in the container
  make -f Makefile.docker build    # rebuild from the mounted source tree
                                   # into ./bld
